      ":question/id": "9139630e-0984-55e3-9206-03a6b70b610c",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+4)}^{10}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u={x}^{2}+4.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+4)}^{10}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{({x}^{2}+4)}^{10}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{10}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{10}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{9{u}^{9}})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18{u}^{9}}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18({x}^{2}+4)^{9}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
