      ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{x}{(6-{x}^{2})^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=6-{x}^{2}.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2x\\,\u27f9\\,(-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{(6-{x}^{2})}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{(6-{x}^{2})}^{5}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{{u}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(-\\frac{1}{4{u}^{4}})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8{u}^{4}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8(6-{x}^{2})^{4}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
